{"name":"Caught Red-Handed","hex":"#be4236","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caught red-handed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of catch red-handed"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caught_red-handed"}],"entries":[{"title":"In flagrante delicto","blocks":[{"text":"In flagrante delicto, sometimes simply in flagrante, is a legal term used to indicate that a criminal has been caught in the act of committing an offence. The colloquial \"caught red-handed\" is an English equivalent."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/In_flagranti_%28Emblemata_Horatiana_1607%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_flagrante_delicto","wikidata":"Q284378"},{"title":"Caught","blocks":[{"text":"Caught is a method of dismissing a batsman in cricket. A batsman is out caught if the batsman hits the ball, from a legitimate delivery, with the bat, and the ball is caught by the bowler or a fielder before it hits the ground."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/In_the_air.jpg/330px-In_the_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caught","wikidata":"Q705379"},{"title":"Red-Handed","blocks":[{"text":"\"Red-Handed\" is the 15th episode of the American fairy tale/drama television series Once Upon a Time, which aired in the United States on ABC on March 11, 2012."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-Handed","wikidata":"Q7303422"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Shane_Bond_catching_Mohammad_Yousuf%2C_Dunedin%2C_NZ%2C_2009.jpg/500px-Shane_Bond_catching_Mohammad_Yousuf%2C_Dunedin%2C_NZ%2C_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Shane_Bond_catching_M